{"parentUuid":"853d567b-859e-4148-bf3a-a4fba91264b7","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"b0530d39-334c-4d81-b949-0367cf262803","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"robust-napping-matsumoto","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01CtAmSkSmz599c8j9Xrb3Sa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_015ucTZpdz4GroLoXtiQAzke","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/pandas-excel-processing.md","content":"# Pandas Excel Data Processing\n\n## Overview\nUsing pandas to read and process large Excel files with structured data.\n\n## Installation\n```bash\npip install pandas openpyxl\n```\n\n## Reading Excel Files\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Read specific sheet\ndf = pd.read_excel('file.xlsx', sheet_name='Data', header=None)\n\n# Skip header rows and set proper column names\ndf = pd.read_excel('file.xlsx', sheet_name='Data', header=None, skiprows=9)\ndf.columns = ['col1', 'col2', ...]\n```\n\n## Key Patterns\n- Use `header=None` when headers are not in the first row\n- Use `skiprows` to skip metadata rows\n- Use `.iloc[]` for positional access\n- Use `.groupby()` for aggregation by game/turn numbers\n- Use vectorized operations for performance on large datasets (6000+ rows)\n\n## Data Selection\n```python\n# Select specific columns by position\nrolls = df.iloc[:, 4:10]  # Columns for Roll 1-6\n\n# Filter by condition\nodd_turns = df[df['turn_number'] % 2 == 1]\n```\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":245,"cache_read_input_tokens":47871,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":245,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtCKg26wG71fKewd1zR3","type":"assistant","uuid":"519e6728-7f99-44af-9cc0-030e575e1826","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:58:37.409Z"}
{"parentUuid":"519e6728-7f99-44af-9cc0-030e575e1826","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"b0530d39-334c-4d81-b949-0367cf262803","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"robust-napping-matsumoto","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01CtAmSkSmz599c8j9Xrb3Sa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_017r5zbTUTws2hDQJPNuAFC9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/dice-game-scoring.md","content":"# Dice Game Scoring System\n\n## Overview\nScoring system for a dice game where each turn consists of 6 dice rolls (d6). Each game has 2 turns, and scoring is optimized across both turns.\n\n## Scoring Categories\n\n### 1. High and Often\n- **Score**: highest number rolled × count of that number\n- Example: rolls [1,6,5,5,1,2] → highest=6, count of 6=1, score=6×1=6\n\n### 2. Summation\n- **Score**: sum of all six dice\n- Example: rolls [1,6,5,5,1,2] → score=20\n\n### 3. Highs and Lows\n- **Score**: highest × lowest × (highest - lowest)\n- Example: rolls [1,6,5,5,1,2] → 6 × 1 × (6-1) = 30\n\n### 4. Only Two Numbers\n- **Criteria**: All six rolls consist of exactly two distinct numbers\n- **Score**: 30 (fixed)\n- Example: [3,6,3,6,6,6] → score=30\n\n### 5. All the Numbers\n- **Criteria**: Rolls contain all of 1,2,3,4,5,6 (in any order)\n- **Score**: 40 (fixed)\n\n### 6. Ordered Four\n- **Criteria**: When listed in order rolled, contains a run of 4 consecutive increasing or decreasing numbers\n- **Score**: 50 (fixed)\n- Example: [1,2,3,4,x,x] or [5,4,3,2,x,x] → score=50\n\n## Game Scoring\n- Each game has 2 turns\n- Find highest combined score from both turns\n- Each category can only be used ONCE across both turns\n- Optimize assignment of categories to turns to maximize total score\n\n## Implementation Notes\n```python\ndef score_turn(rolls):\n    \"\"\"Return dict of {category: score} for all valid categories.\"\"\"\n    scores = {}\n\n    # High and Often\n    highest = max(rolls)\n    count = rolls.count(highest)\n    scores['high_often'] = highest * count\n\n    # Summation\n    scores['summation'] = sum(rolls)\n\n    # Highs and Lows\n    hi, lo = max(rolls), min(rolls)\n    scores['highs_lows'] = hi * lo * (hi - lo)\n\n    # Only Two Numbers\n    if len(set(rolls)) == 2:\n        scores['only_two'] = 30\n\n    # All the Numbers\n    if set(rolls) == {1,2,3,4,5,6}:\n        scores['all_numbers'] = 40\n\n    # Ordered Four\n    if has_run_of_4(rolls):\n        scores['ordered_four'] = 50\n\n    return scores\n```\n\n## Optimal Game Score\nUse itertools or dynamic programming to find best category assignment:\n- For each turn, compute all possible category scores\n- Try all pairs of different categories for the two turns\n- Return maximum combined score\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":245,"cache_read_input_tokens":47871,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":245,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtCKg26wG71fKewd1zR3","type":"assistant","uuid":"d2805abb-fffb-466e-8f01-a23c22d7f9ca","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:58:50.679Z"}
{"parentUuid":"d2805abb-fffb-466e-8f01-a23c22d7f9ca","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"b0530d39-334c-4d81-b949-0367cf262803","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"robust-napping-matsumoto","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01CtAmSkSmz599c8j9Xrb3Sa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01LBkzwqzei8dU5Gm1Tz6qgL","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/combinatorial-optimization-game-matching.md","content":"# Combinatorial Optimization for Game Matching\n\n## Overview\nMatching players in a tournament-style setup where games are assigned to players based on game number parity, then paired off.\n\n## Player Assignment Pattern\n- **Player 1**: plays odd-numbered games (game 1, 3, 5, ...)\n- **Player 2**: plays even-numbered games (game 2, 4, 6, ...)\n- **Match pairing**: game 1 vs game 2, game 3 vs game 4, etc.\n\n## Implementation\n```python\n# With 3000 games: 1500 odd, 1500 even → 1500 matches\nplayer1_games = [g for g in games if g['game_number'] % 2 == 1]  # games 1,3,5,...\nplayer2_games = [g for g in games if g['game_number'] % 2 == 0]  # games 2,4,6,...\n\n# Match: player1_games[i] vs player2_games[i]\n# (game 1 vs game 2, game 3 vs game 4, etc.)\n\np1_wins = 0\np2_wins = 0\nfor i in range(len(player1_games)):\n    if player1_games[i]['score'] > player2_games[i]['score']:\n        p1_wins += 1\n    elif player2_games[i]['score'] > player1_games[i]['score']:\n        p2_wins += 1\n    # ties: neither wins\n\nanswer = p1_wins - p2_wins\n```\n\n## Key Considerations\n- Game scores must be computed optimally (best category assignment across 2 turns per game)\n- Ties don't count for either player\n- Total matches = number of games / 2 = 1500\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":245,"cache_read_input_tokens":47871,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":245,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtCKg26wG71fKewd1zR3","type":"assistant","uuid":"e1f643b4-ce5f-4b50-a16f-204db983a30a","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:58:58.194Z"}
{"parentUuid":"e1f643b4-ce5f-4b50-a16f-204db983a30a","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"b0530d39-334c-4d81-b949-0367cf262803","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"robust-napping-matsumoto","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01CtAmSkSmz599c8j9Xrb3Sa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01HRKyADK7L7ZEdVgL98VyPz","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/run-of-consecutive-detection.md","content":"# Detecting Runs of Consecutive Numbers in Sequences\n\n## Overview\nDetecting whether a sequence of numbers contains a subsequence (contiguous) of 4 consecutive increasing or decreasing numbers.\n\n## Algorithm\nFor a sequence of 6 dice rolls, check all windows of size 4:\n- Windows: [0:4], [1:5], [2:6]\n- For each window, check if it forms an increasing or decreasing sequence with step size 1\n\n## Implementation\n```python\ndef has_run_of_4(rolls):\n    \"\"\"Check if rolls contain a run of 4 consecutive increasing or decreasing numbers.\"\"\"\n    for i in range(len(rolls) - 3):\n        window = rolls[i:i+4]\n        # Check increasing: each element is exactly 1 more than previous\n        if all(window[j+1] - window[j] == 1 for j in range(3)):\n            return True\n        # Check decreasing: each element is exactly 1 less than previous\n        if all(window[j] - window[j+1] == 1 for j in range(3)):\n            return True\n    return False\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n- The run must be **contiguous in the original roll order** (not sorted)\n- \"Consecutive\" means step of exactly 1 (e.g., 2-3-4-5, not 1-3-5-7)\n- Both increasing AND decreasing runs qualify\n- The run of 4 must appear as a substring of the 6-roll sequence\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":245,"cache_read_input_tokens":47871,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":245,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtCKg26wG71fKewd1zR3","type":"assistant","uuid":"02f2c270-0ff5-47d3-89e1-74b1b3689d0c","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:59:04.307Z"}
{"parentUuid":"02f2c270-0ff5-47d3-89e1-74b1b3689d0c","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"b0530d39-334c-4d81-b949-0367cf262803","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"robust-napping-matsumoto","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01CtAmSkSmz599c8j9Xrb3Sa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01CUVszxeKT1rJsDk7sJLq9R","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/optimal-category-assignment.md","content":"# Optimal Category Assignment for Two-Turn Dice Game\n\n## Problem\nGiven two turns in a game, each with multiple possible category scores, find the maximum combined score where each category is used at most once.\n\n## Approach\nSince there are only 6 categories, we can enumerate all valid pairs:\n- For turn 1, try each available category\n- For turn 2, try each remaining category\n- Track the maximum combined score\n\n## Implementation\n```python\nfrom itertools import product\n\ndef optimal_game_score(turn1_scores, turn2_scores):\n    \"\"\"\n    turn1_scores: dict of {category: score}\n    turn2_scores: dict of {category: score}\n    Returns: maximum combined score\n    \"\"\"\n    best = 0\n\n    # Try all combinations of (category for turn1, category for turn2)\n    for cat1, score1 in turn1_scores.items():\n        for cat2, score2 in turn2_scores.items():\n            if cat1 != cat2:  # Categories must be different\n                best = max(best, score1 + score2)\n\n    return best\n```\n\n## Edge Cases\n- A turn might not qualify for certain categories (e.g., \"Only Two Numbers\" requires exactly 2 distinct values)\n- If a turn qualifies for no special categories, it still has High and Often, Summation, and Highs and Lows\n- Every turn always qualifies for at least: High and Often, Summation, Highs and Lows (3 categories)\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":245,"cache_read_input_